  "type": "biological",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p>Bouncers are genetically adapted for microgravity. Their legs are more limber and their feet can grasp as well as their hands. They can tolerate the cold temperatures of beehive tunnels and have an oxygen reserve in case they are exposed to vacuum. Bouncers are very common in the outer system and zero-g habitats.</p>",
